WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.922 --> 00:00:14.744
I exclaimed, blurting out my story idea.

2
00:00:14.764 --> 00:00:19.725
"Let's write a story about a giant talking vacuum cleaner.

3
00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:22.206
It can suck up the whole world!"

4
00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:27.587
Molly blinked at me.

5
00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:29.708
Then she shook her head.

6
00:00:30.808 --> 00:00:31.449
"No, Iggy.

7
00:00:31.909 --> 00:00:34.110
The vaccum cleaner sounds like a monster.

8
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.851
I'm not writing a story about a monster!"

9
00:00:39.053 --> 00:00:41.434
At lunch we talked some more about my idea.

10
00:00:42.495 --> 00:00:44.616
Molly kept pointing out problems with it.

11
00:00:45.656 --> 00:00:50.199
"The giant vacuum cleaner can't suck up the whole world, Iggy," she said.

12
00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:55.001
"If it did, there wouldn't be a story because nothing would be left."

13
00:00:56.362 --> 00:00:57.663
I knew Molly was right.

14
00:01:00.404 --> 00:01:05.106
I decided that thinking of a plot for a story was even harder than inventing!

15
00:01:06.206 --> 00:01:08.547
Other kids were talking about plot ideas too.

16
00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:14.408
"Mrs. Romano said we should bounce our ideas off each other," said Colby.

17
00:01:14.428 --> 00:01:19.830
"Boing!" said Jake, bouncing a grape off Colby's head.

18
00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:24.232
"She said to bounce story ideas, not food!"

19
00:01:24.692 --> 00:01:26.524
said Kristin.

20
00:01:26.564 --> 00:01:31.146
After school we stopped at Molly's apartment to ask if Molly could come to my apartment.

21
00:01:33.087 --> 00:01:37.068
Caswell and Lucy were in the living room, watching Monster Madness again.

22
00:01:40.029 --> 00:01:42.010
Lucy just stared at the TV screen.

23
00:01:43.131 --> 00:01:46.612
"Iggy, your mom wants to see you and Molly right away.

24
00:01:46.632 --> 00:01:48.113
She has a surprise."

25
00:01:50.414 --> 00:01:52.594
Molly and I raced over to my apartment.

26
00:01:52.614 --> 00:01:55.115
"What's the surprise, Mom?"

27
00:01:55.436 --> 00:01:56.196
I blurted out.

28
00:01:57.556 --> 00:01:59.917
"I can't tell you yet," said Mom.

29
00:01:59.937 --> 00:02:02.579
"But we're going somewhere fun.

30
00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:05.000
Caswell can come too, if he wants."

31
00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.402
Caswell decided he could miss the rest of Monster Madness for today.

32
00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:16.725
Soon all of us, including Lucy, were walking down the busy street.

33
00:02:18.526 --> 00:02:21.208
We passed Bubbles Bath Shop and waved to Mr.

34
00:02:21.268 --> 00:02:26.389
Chen. We passed our school and waved to Mrs.

35
00:02:26.449 --> 00:02:28.909
Romano, who was just leaving for the day.

36
00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:34.371
At last my mom stopped in front of a shop I had never seen before.

37
00:02:35.691 --> 00:02:38.892
A sign read: "Garden Gate Children's Bookstore.

38
00:02:39.352 --> 00:02:41.013
Author Story Hour Today!"

39
00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:44.774
"It's a new bookstore," my mom explained.

40
00:02:44.794 --> 00:02:48.355
"And we're just in time for story hour."

41
00:02:49.515 --> 00:02:52.496
We entered through a door that looked like a garden gate.

42
00:02:55.528 --> 00:02:59.912
Kids were sitting on the floor, and a lady was sitting on a chair in front of them.

43
00:02:59.932 --> 00:03:03.936
"I'm Matilda Mackey," she said.

44
00:03:03.956 --> 00:03:09.360
"I'm going to read my new book, The Wicky Wacky School."

45
00:03:12.023 --> 00:03:15.966
Matilda Mackey's book was about a school where weird things happen.

46
00:03:17.087 --> 00:03:21.951
One day the teachers turn into monkeys, and the main character has to figure out how to change

47
00:03:21.991 --> 00:03:22.452
them back.

48
00:03:23.508 --> 00:03:28.331
She solves the problem when she realizes the teachers have been eating too many bananas.

49
00:03:30.513 --> 00:03:34.315
I thought the story was really funny and had a lot of suspense.

50
00:03:35.536 --> 00:03:37.577
Suddenly I got an idea.

51
00:03:38.358 --> 00:03:39.639
I leaned over to Molly.

52
00:03:39.659 --> 00:03:41.560
"Maybe Mrs.

53
00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.542
Mackey can help us think of a plot for our story!"

54
00:03:45.603 --> 00:03:48.205
Molly nodded and gave me the thumbs-up sign.

55
00:03:49.485 --> 00:03:50.026
After Mrs.

56
00:03:50.086 --> 00:03:53.128
Mackey finished reading, Molly and I rushed up to her.

57
00:03:54.292 --> 00:03:55.894
"My name is Iggy," I said.

58
00:03:55.914 --> 00:03:57.555
"I'm an inventor."

59
00:03:57.575 --> 00:04:00.678
"And I'm Molly," said Molly.

60
00:04:00.698 --> 00:04:02.680
"I'm just a regular person."

61
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.864
"We're writing a story in school," I explained.

62
00:04:06.884 --> 00:04:10.908
"And we can't think of a good plot," added Molly.

63
00:04:12.129 --> 00:04:14.352
Mrs. Mackey's eyes lit up.

64
00:04:15.853 --> 00:04:18.496
"Here's what you have to do," she said.

65
00:04:19.568 --> 00:04:23.570
"Ask yourself what the character wants more than anything in the world.

66
00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:27.171
And then give her a huge problem to solve."

67
00:04:28.472 --> 00:04:29.852
Somehow Mrs.

68
00:04:29.932 --> 00:04:32.033
Mackey's words sounded familiar.

69
00:04:33.254 --> 00:04:34.614
Then I realized why.

70
00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:37.115
It was just like my life!

71
00:04:37.575 --> 00:04:40.237
I always wanted to invent things to help people.

72
00:04:41.477 --> 00:04:46.479
And I always had a huge problem: my inventions turned out to be flops!
